    "title": "החגיגה המשפחתית",
    "description": "Tokyo Dome City, זמן משפחתי וארוחת חגיגה",
    "category": "mitzvah",
    "html": "<h1>07 — Family Celebration Day</h1>\n<p><strong>Date:</strong> Saturday, October 10, 2026\n<strong>Location:</strong> Tokyo Dome City\n<strong>Goal:</strong> a personal, playful celebration for the 12-year-old—not another packed sightseeing day.</p>\n<h2>Why Tokyo Dome City Wins</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>It matches his gaming/ride interests.</li>\n<li>The family can stay in one compact area.</li>\n<li>Rides, karaoke, JUMP SHOP, bowling/arcade and dinner can flex around weather.</li>\n<li>It avoids crossing Tokyo between unrelated “special” activities.</li>\n<li>It feels celebratory without forcing a formal event the child may not want.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>The Day</h2>\n<h3>Slow morning</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Sleep in.</li>\n<li>Have a proper brunch.</li>\n<li>Give the family gift privately.</li>\n<li>Let him choose the first ride/activity.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Afternoon headline</h3>\n<p>At <strong>Tokyo Dome City Attractions</strong>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Thunder Dolphin for anyone who wants it and meets the current restrictions.</li>\n<li>Big-O Ferris wheel; request/choose a karaoke gondola if available.</li>\n<li>One JUMP SHOP keepsake with a pre-agreed budget.</li>\n<li>Bowling or arcade only if the weather affects rides or the family wants more play.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Check live ride operations and maintenance on the <a href=\"https://www.at-raku.com/\">official attractions site</a>.</p>\n<p>The Miyamoto bachi bought after Taiko-kan on Oct 16 is a separate, personal drumming keepsake. It complements this celebration day; it does not need to replace the family gift.</p>\n<h3>Evening</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Reserve a restaurant near Tokyo Dome, Kagurazaka or the accommodation.</li>\n<li>Ask in advance for a dessert message.</li>\n<li>Keep a short private family moment: each person says one thing they admire about him and one wish for the year ahead.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What Not to Add</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>No cross-city viewpoint.</li>\n<li>No second major museum.</li>\n<li>No shopping district.</li>\n<li>No Tokyo Yosakoi preview. The next morning starts with an early Kyoto transfer.</li>\n<li>No formal ceremony unless the son specifically requests one.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Weather Versions</h2>\n<h3>Dry</h3>\n<p>Rides → Big-O → JUMP SHOP → dinner.</p>\n<h3>Wet</h3>\n<p>Indoor game/bowling block → Big-O if operating → JUMP SHOP → early dinner or private karaoke.</p>\n<h2>Booking Checklist</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><input disabled=\"\" type=\"checkbox\"> Ask the son privately whether he prefers rides, bowling or karaoke as the headline.</li>\n<li><input disabled=\"\" type=\"checkbox\"> Reserve dinner.</li>\n<li><input disabled=\"\" type=\"checkbox\"> Request a dessert message and confirm any dietary needs.</li>\n<li><input disabled=\"\" type=\"checkbox\"> Buy/wrap the family gift before travel.</li>\n<li><input disabled=\"\" type=\"checkbox\"> Recheck attraction maintenance one week before.</li>\n<li><input disabled=\"\" type=\"checkbox\"> Keep the morning empty in the calendar.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Budget Envelope</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th align=\"right\">Planning range</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Attractions / rides for four</td>\n<td align=\"right\">JPY 10,000–20,000</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>JUMP SHOP keepsake</td>\n<td align=\"right\">JPY 3,000–8,000</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Celebration dinner</td>\n<td align=\"right\">JPY 16,000–32,000</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Dessert/message or karaoke extra</td>\n<td align=\"right\">JPY 3,000–8,000</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Day envelope excluding gift</strong></td>\n<td align=\"right\"><strong>JPY 32,000–68,000</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The emotional target is simple: he gets a day that feels chosen for him, the sister still has fun, and nobody is exhausted before the early Kyoto train, Mizuekai and Awata the next morning.</p>\n",
    "markdown": "# 07 — Family Celebration Day\n\n**Date:** Saturday, October 10, 2026\n**Location:** Tokyo Dome City\n**Goal:** a personal, playful celebration for the 12-year-old—not another packed sightseeing day.\n\n## Why Tokyo Dome City Wins\n\n- It matches his gaming/ride interests.\n- The family can stay in one compact area.\n- Rides, karaoke, JUMP SHOP, bowling/arcade and dinner can flex around weather.\n- It avoids crossing Tokyo between unrelated “special” activities.\n- It feels celebratory without forcing a formal event the child may not want.\n\n## The Day\n\n### Slow morning\n\n- Sleep in.\n- Have a proper brunch.\n- Give the family gift privately.\n- Let him choose the first ride/activity.\n\n### Afternoon headline\n\nAt **Tokyo Dome City Attractions**:\n\n1. Thunder Dolphin for anyone who wants it and meets the current restrictions.\n2. Big-O Ferris wheel; request/choose a karaoke gondola if available.\n3. One JUMP SHOP keepsake with a pre-agreed budget.\n4. Bowling or arcade only if the weather affects rides or the family wants more play.\n\nCheck live ride operations and maintenance on the [official attractions site](https://www.at-raku.com/).\n\nThe Miyamoto bachi bought after Taiko-kan on Oct 16 is a separate, personal drumming keepsake. It complements this celebration day; it does not need to replace the family gift.\n\n### Evening\n\n- Reserve a restaurant near Tokyo Dome, Kagurazaka or the accommodation.\n- Ask in advance for a dessert message.\n- Keep a short private family moment: each person says one thing they admire about him and one wish for the year ahead.\n\n## What Not to Add\n\n- No cross-city viewpoint.\n- No second major museum.\n- No shopping district.\n- No Tokyo Yosakoi preview. The next morning starts with an early Kyoto transfer.\n- No formal ceremony unless the son specifically requests one.\n\n## Weather Versions\n\n### Dry\n\nRides → Big-O → JUMP SHOP → dinner.\n\n### Wet\n\nIndoor game/bowling block → Big-O if operating → JUMP SHOP → early dinner or private karaoke.\n\n## Booking Checklist\n\n- [ ] Ask the son privately whether he prefers rides, bowling or karaoke as the headline.\n- [ ] Reserve dinner.\n- [ ] Request a dessert message and confirm any dietary needs.\n- [ ] Buy/wrap the family gift before travel.\n- [ ] Recheck attraction maintenance one week before.\n- [ ] Keep the morning empty in the calendar.\n\n## Budget Envelope\n\n| Item | Planning range |\n|---|---:|\n| Attractions / rides for four | JPY 10,000–20,000 |\n| JUMP SHOP keepsake | JPY 3,000–8,000 |\n| Celebration dinner | JPY 16,000–32,000 |\n| Dessert/message or karaoke extra | JPY 3,000–8,000 |\n| **Day envelope excluding gift** | **JPY 32,000–68,000** |\n\nThe emotional target is simple: he gets a day that feels chosen for him, the sister still has fun, and nobody is exhausted before the early Kyoto train, Mizuekai and Awata the next morning.\n"
